-Only an `UP` click can end capture in this mode. `DOWN` and `OK` gestures
-that begin or trigger during capture are suppressed. A fresh press can trigger
+An `UP` click ends capture normally. Capture suppresses editing gestures.
+With `"cancelVoice":true` in `host_ready`, an OK hold within the same
+active capture stops the microphone and sends the following terminal event.
+
+```json
+{"v":1,"type":"ptt_cancel","sessionId":123,"seq":1}
+```
+
+The host discards buffered audio for that session and sends `host_state`
+with `state:"ready"` after cancellation completes. An OK press that starts
+during capture is consumed by that capture. A fresh press can trigger
 immediately after `UP` requests the stop. The audio worker queues its
 `button_event` after successfully queueing `ptt_up`, with an optional
 `sessionId` identifying the capture if the gesture triggered before
